args.command:
cat > /tmp/fix.pl <<'PERL'
s{\Q| 1 | `orders` / read | readers = owner + recipient at creation | Any authenticated non-owner can read another user's order note/detail |\E}{| 1 | `orders` / read | readers = owner + recipient at creation | Tested authenticated non-owner (`user-bob`) reads another user's order note/detail |}g;
s{\Q| 2 | `orders` / update | writers = owner; sharing = read only | Any authenticated non-owner (including a non-recipient) can modify another user's order |\E}{| 2 | `orders` / update | writers = owner; sharing = read only | Tested authenticated non-owners (`user-bob`, `user-admin`) modify another user's order; recipient and non-recipient both observed |}g;
s{\Q| 3 | `stale_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | After an owner read, any authenticated user or anonymous/invalid-session requester reads the cached note/detail |\E}{| 3 | `stale_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | After an owner read, tested authenticated users and anonymous/invalid-session requesters read the cached note/detail |}g;
s{\Q| 4 | `forbidden_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | Non-owner and anonymous requesters receive note/detail in the `403` response body |\E}{| 4 | `forbidden_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | Tested non-owner and anonymous requesters receive note/detail in the `403` response body |}g;
s{\Q| 5 | `echo_reports` / read | readers = owner | Global `echoes` list discloses other users' notes; path id is ignored and no session is required |\E}{| 5 | `echo_reports` / read | readers = owner | Global `echoes` list discloses tested users' notes; path id is ignored and no session is required |}g;
s{\Q| 6 | `private_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | Unauthenticated/invalid-session requesters read note/detail; authenticated non-owners are denied |\E}{| 6 | `private_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | Tested unauthenticated/invalid-session requesters read note/detail; authenticated non-owners are denied |}g;
s{\Q- **Identity and absence controls:** `GET /app/api/me` returned the expected stable IDs for alice, bob, and admin. Unknown ids on each class returned `404` (except the documented public reads and the `login_reports`/`echo_reports` exceptions noted above). Anonymous requests to protected classes returned `401` where expected.\E}{- **Identity and absence controls:** `GET /app/api/me` returned the expected stable IDs for alice, bob, and admin. Unknown ids returned `404` for every tested class except `echo_reports` (which ignores the id and returned `200`); `login_reports` returned `404` for unknown ids but `200` for an existing-inaccessible id (see the observation below). Anonymous requests to protected classes returned `401` where expected.}g;
PERL
cd /workspace && perl -0777 -i /tmp/fix.pl report.md
sed -n '18,30p' report.md; grep -n "Identity and absence" report.md

cat > /tmp/fix.awk <<'AWK'
NR==22 { print "| 1 | `orders` / read | readers = owner + recipient at creation | Tested authenticated non-owner (`user-bob`) reads another user's order note/detail |"; next }
NR==23 { print "| 2 | `orders` / update | writers = owner; sharing = read only | Tested authenticated non-owners (`user-bob`, `user-admin`) modify another user's order; recipient and non-recipient both observed |"; next }
NR==24 { print "| 3 | `stale_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | After an owner read, tested authenticated users and anonymous/invalid-session requesters read the cached note/detail |"; next }
NR==25 { print "| 4 | `forbidden_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | Tested non-owner and anonymous requesters receive note/detail in the `403` response body |"; next }
NR==26 { print "| 5 | `echo_reports` / read | readers = owner | Global `echoes` list discloses tested users' notes; path id is ignored and no session is required |"; next }
NR==27 { print "| 6 | `private_reports` / read | readers = owner; 401 without session | Tested unauthenticated/invalid-session requesters read note/detail; authenticated non-owners are denied |"; next }
NR==320 { print "- **Identity and absence controls:** `GET /app/api/me` returned the expected stable IDs for alice, bob, and admin. Unknown ids returned `404` for every tested class except `echo_reports` (which ignores the id and returned `200`); `login_reports` returned `404` for unknown ids but `200` for an existing-inaccessible id (see the observation below). Anonymous requests to protected classes returned `401` where expected."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '18,30p' report.md; grep -n "Identity and absence" report.md

cat > /tmp/fix2.awk <<'AWK'
NR==163 { print "  - The leaked response was freshly generated (`Date` changed per request) and still declared `cache-control: no-store`; this is not a replay of a cached HTTP response by the proxy. The in-scope target itself returned the stale content."; next }
NR==164 { print "- **Limits / qualifications:** the leak requires a prior successful owner read to populate the cache. It was observed immediately after that read and persisted for at least ~80–120 seconds; the exact TTL/eviction policy was not determined. The disclosed response was not scoped to the requester: tested authenticated users, an anonymous request, and an invalid-session request all received the same body. The leak is read-only: non-owner update/delete remained `404`/`401`, and owner deletion invalidated the entry. No claim is made about cache behavior after a process restart."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix2.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '158,166p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix3.awk <<'AWK'
NR==295 { print; print "  - Anonymous `GET /app/api/me` on the same no-Cookie transport returned `401 {\"error\":\"authentication_required\"}`, confirming the private read is not a proxy-injected identity."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix3.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '292,300p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix4.awk <<'AWK'
NR==58 { print; print "  - No-prior-owner-read control: alice created order `d5217c0b-e736-4357-83e1-a1cc4ecf9180`; bob's `GET` before any alice read returned `200` with note `EVID-ORD-NOOWNERREAD-1795454098` / detail `D-1795454098`."; next }
NR==96 { print; print "  - No-prior-owner-read control: bob `PATCH`ed order `d5217c0b-e736-4357-83e1-a1cc4ecf9180` before any alice read; returned `204`, and alice's subsequent `GET` returned `200` with `EVID-ORD-NOOWNERREAD-BOB-1795454098`."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix4.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '55,60p' report.md; echo '---'; sed -n '95,100p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix5.awk <<'AWK'
NR==197 { print "  - The same behavior was reproduced with a second object and no prior owner read: `24ae090c-41b7-4773-becb-9abade0acfe5`, note `EVID-FORBID-C-1795453861`, detail `DFC-1795453861`, was created by alice and then returned with `403` and the full body to an explicit-empty-`Cookie:` request."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix5.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '195,199p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix6.awk <<'AWK'
NR==254 { print "- **Limits / qualifications:** `echo_reports` returns only `note` values in the `echoes` array; `detail` is not echoed by this class. The array is global and persisted across sessions/users; later captures showed older entries dropping out, so it appears bounded/rolling. The exact retention policy was not determined. No cross-user write/delete was observed. The read is also unauthenticated."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix6.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '252,256p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix7.awk <<'AWK'
{ print }
END { print ""; print "- The final `### Final reproducibility smoke test` section in the log re-confirms Findings 1–6 with fresh objects." }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix7.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
tail -8 report.md

cat > /tmp/fix8.awk <<'AWK'
NR==13 { print "- **Method:** for each resource class, created distinct marker objects and exercised owner read/update/delete baselines, authenticated non-owner access (primarily `bob`, with `admin` on the affected classes and as a control), anonymous no-cookie access, invalid-session-cookie access, unknown-object `404` controls, and sharing controls. Full raw request/response capture is in `/workspace/evidence.log`."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix8.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '11,15p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix9.awk <<'AWK'
NR==164 { print; print "  - Alice's sharing state was `{\"share_new_with\":null}` (the leak did not depend on sharing)."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix9.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '162,167p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix10.awk <<'AWK'
NR==27 { print; print ""; print "**Conclusion:** six supported authorization findings (Findings 1–6) are reported above. The remaining tested classes and operations matched their declared rules within the stated limits; the `login_reports` and `expiring_reports` observations are not submitted as cross-user findings."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix10.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '24,33p' report.md

cat > /tmp/fix11.awk <<'AWK'
NR==5 { print; print "- **Authorized effects:** authenticate with the supplied exploration accounts and create/read/update/delete in-scope fixture objects, as declared in `engagement.json`."; next }
{ print }
AWK
cd /workspace && awk -f /tmp/fix11.awk report.md > report.new && mv report.new report.md
sed -n '3,8p' report.md
